WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.169
(Robert): Rebellion!

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.170
The crimes of House Targaryen
were too heinous to go unanswered.

00:00:11.301 --> 00:00:15.345
The noble Houses of Baratheon,
Stark, and Arryn,

00:00:15.346 --> 00:00:20.346
united to oppose and overthrow
the line of the cursed dragon kings.

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:26.186
While Ned Stark and Arryn secured
an alliance with the Tullys of Riverrun,

00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.359
I called the banners of Storm's End

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.198
and rode out in force against the Mad King
and his minions.

00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:38.035
Gods, those were some battles!

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:40.704
Our first victory occurred at Summerhall

00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:43.707
where I faced off against
an army of dragon loyalists

00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:46.293
and won three battles in a single day -

00:00:46.294 --> 00:00:48.670
three in one day!

00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:52.216
Seven hells, that was a glorious day!

00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:55.093
We tried to take Ashford Castle 
in the Reach,

00:00:55.094 --> 00:00:57.888
but the Tyrells beat us back.

00:00:57.889 --> 00:00:59.890
We had to regroup.

00:00:59.891 --> 00:01:03.227
My army was pursued north by Aerys' army

00:01:03.228 --> 00:01:07.523
and took refuge in the Stoney Sept
in the riverlands.

00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:09.942
When the Targaryen army entered the town,

00:01:09.943 --> 00:01:11.818
the sept bells tolled,

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:16.073
a signal to the townspeople
of the battle that was to come.

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:19.618
As the Targaryens searched
from house to house for me,

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:24.619
the combined forces of Ned Stark
and the Tullys swept into the city.

00:01:24.707 --> 00:01:28.085
Gods, what a day that was!

00:01:28.086 --> 00:01:32.214
It's now known as the Battle of the Bells.

00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:35.217
We overwhelmed the Mad King's forces

00:01:35.218 --> 00:01:39.638
and sent them scampering
back to King's Landing.

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:43.767
Aerys' son, Rhaegar,
who started the whole damn thing,

00:01:43.768 --> 00:01:46.603
finally emerged from hiding in the South,

00:01:46.604 --> 00:01:49.856
and assembled his own army to face us.

00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:54.857
As for the Mad King,
he must have been pissing himself.

00:01:54.946 --> 00:01:58.198
The battle that would decide the fate
of the Seven Kingdoms

00:01:58.199 --> 00:02:03.199
occurred at the crossing of the Green Fork
of the Trident river.

00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:08.329
Rhaegar commanded the royal host,
which was some 40,000 strong.

00:02:08.585 --> 00:02:13.046
My forces were outnumbered
by nearly 5,000 men,

00:02:13.047 --> 00:02:15.340
but that didn't matter.

00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:17.050
They were fresh,

00:02:17.051 --> 00:02:22.051
but we were battle hardened
and had justice on our side.

00:02:22.473 --> 00:02:27.144
As the battle raged around us,
I faced off with Rhaegar -

00:02:27.145 --> 00:02:31.815
the stag and the dragon
right there in the ford of the river.

00:02:31.816 --> 00:02:34.568
I fought with the fury of ten men,

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:38.071
raining blow after blow 
upon that vile prince

00:02:38.072 --> 00:02:41.825
before burying my war hammer in his chest.

00:02:41.826 --> 00:02:45.162
I hit him so hard,
the rubies on his armor broke free,

00:02:45.163 --> 00:02:47.164
flinging them into the stream.

00:02:47.165 --> 00:02:50.417
They call it the Ruby Ford now.

00:02:50.418 --> 00:02:55.005
With that scum Rhaegar dead
and the royal army shattered,

00:02:55.006 --> 00:02:58.842
our next move was 
to make for King's Landing.

00:02:58.843 --> 00:03:03.430
But I'd sustained a few wounds 
in the battle and was unable to ride.

00:03:03.431 --> 00:03:05.599
I sent Ned Stark to the capital

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.600
to face the Mad King
and make him pay for his crimes.

